From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: stop disabling the pipe clock it does not own

Second half of the fix; applies on top of the companion patch
0531-phy-qcom-qmp-combo-replay-shared-com-setup-after-sleep.patch.

qmp_combo_usb_power_on() drops qmp->pipe_clk on its error path, but that
clock is taken by qmp_combo_com_init() and given back by
qmp_combo_com_exit(), which qmp_combo_usb_init() calls right after a
failed power-on. When a second user - the DP sub-PHY - holds the
init_count reference, com_exit() correctly leaves the clock alone, so
power-on()'s extra disable fires on a clock that is already off:

    gcc_usb3_prim_phy_pipe_clk already disabled
    gcc_usb3_prim_phy_pipe_clk already unprepared

and leaves the shared block with a stale pipe clock for the next attempt,
hiding the real failure behind a pair of warnings. Drop the error path and
let the caller's com_exit() own the teardown.

Signed-off-by: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
---
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -3940,15 +3940,10 @@
 			qmp->qmpphy_mode, qmp->com_powered);
 		dev_err(qmp->dev, "  qmp refs: usb_init=%u dp_init=%u\n",
 			qmp->usb_init_count, qmp->dp_init_count);
-		goto err_disable_pipe_clk;
+		return ret;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
-
-err_disable_pipe_clk:
-	clk_disable_unprepare(qmp->pipe_clk);
-
-	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qmp_combo_usb_power_off(struct phy *phy)
